{"content":[{"c":["KINNERETH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Fortified town in the territory allotted to Naphtali’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.35","r":"Josh.19.35","rawR":"Josh.19.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.35","value":"Josh.19.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:35"},"). It is also mentioned in an Egyptian list of towns conquered by Thutmose III in the 15th century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". The site has been identified as Tell el-’Oreimeh on the northwest shore of the Sea of Galilee. Archaeological evidence suggests that the site was inhabited from about 2000 to about 900 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. A district in Naphtali’s territory that included #1 above. It was conquered by Ben-hadad, king of Syria, in the reign of Baasha, king of the northern kingdom of Israel in the early ninth century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.15.20","r":"1Kgs.15.20","rawR":"1Kgs.15.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.15.20","value":"1Kgs.15.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 15:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Early name for the Sea of Galilee (",{"href":"?bref=Num.34.11","r":"Num.34.11","rawR":"Num.34.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.34.11","value":"Num.34.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 34:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.17","r":"Deut.3.17","rawR":"Deut.3.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.17","value":"Deut.3.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.2","r":"Josh.11.2","rawR":"Josh.11.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.2","value":"Josh.11.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.3","r":"Josh.12.3","rawR":"Josh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.3","value":"Josh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.27","r":"Josh.13.27","rawR":"Josh.13.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.27","value":"Josh.13.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:27"},"). It is hard to say whether the city (see #1 above) was named after the sea or vice versa. The name, however, means “lyres,” which could be an allusion to the Sea of Galilee’s shape, which roughly resembles that of a lyre. In NT times the pronunciation of the name was corrupted to Gennesaret (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.1","r":"Luke.5.1","rawR":"Luke.5.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.1","value":"Luke.5.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:1"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=SeaofGalilee_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SeaofGalilee_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SeaofGalilee_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sea of Galilee"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Kinnereth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 19:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.35","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.35","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.35"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 15:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.15.20","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.15.20","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.15.20"},{"anchorText":"Nm 34:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.34.11","rawQueryValue":"Num.34.11","sourceRefExact":"Num.34.11"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.17","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.17","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.17"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.2","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.2","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.2"},{"anchorText":"12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.3","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.3","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.3"},{"anchorText":"13:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.27","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.27","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.27"},{"anchorText":"Lk 5:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.5.1","rawQueryValue":"Luke.5.1","sourceRefExact":"Luke.5.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e19c2dc27e191929e8e6782f70605c24c9fbd9b2f9ad696b76628002ef5231e6","sourceItemName":"Kinnereth","sourceItemOrder":89,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Kinnereth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Kinnereth","title":"Kinnereth","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}